.TH GETPID 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getpid \- get the current process ID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B "pid_t getpid(void);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Returns the current Linux process ID. The child of
.BR fork (3crunch)
has a different process ID from its parent.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the process ID. The Linux getpid syscall cannot fail and does not
change Crunch errno.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fork (3crunch),
.BR kill (3crunch),
.BR getpid (2)
